## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to reason about cascading failures in a real-world, multi-region microservices architecture. It evaluates understanding of both preventive controls (rate limits, circuit breakers) and reactive strategies (cache bypass, warmup) with measurable SLOs and fast rollback capabilities.

## Key Concepts

- Per-endpoint rate limiting and circuit breakers for load control
- Cache warmup and controlled rollouts for spike preparation
- Backpressure and producer throttling to regulate traffic flow
- Eviction tuning and failover paths for resilience
- Automated rollback and SLO-driven incident response

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple token bucket limiter (conceptual)
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(capacity, refillRate) {
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.refillRate = refillRate;
    this.lastRefill = Date.now();
  }

  allowRequest() {
    this.refill();
    if (this.tokens >= 1) {
      this.tokens -= 1;
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }

  refill() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.lastRefill) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + elapsed * this.refillRate);
    this.lastRefill = now;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Telemetry quality is critical for root cause analysis and cross-service tracing; this checks practical skills for CI, instrumentation, and rollback safety.

## Key Concepts

- Telemetry integrity, trace propagation, OpenTelemetry, CI gates, canary deployments
- Error budgets and dashboards alignment
- Synthetic validation and fallback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// OpenTelemetry middleware for trace propagation
const { trace, context, propagation } = require('@opentelemetry/api');

function ensureTraceId(req, res, next) {
  const carrier = propagation.createExtractHeadersCarrier(req.headers);
  const ctx = propagation.extract(context.active(), carrier);

  if (!trace.getSpan(ctx).spanContext().traceId) {
    const tracer = trace.getTracer('default');
    const span = tracer.startSpan('fallback-trace');
    propagation.inject(context.active(), carrier);
  }
  next();
}
```

